# Optional. Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) if you want to set the sync
# passcode up front:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # then edit .env
#
# You can leave it unset instead — on first launch the app shows a "Create
# passcode" screen and stores it for you. Either way, the synced dashboard is
# locked until a passcode exists; there are no usernames, this one passcode is
# the whole login, so pick something long.
#
# OPENLOO_PASSCODE=change-me-to-something-long
